    "c2": {
      "anchor": "context",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "1. The whole design, one example",
      "excerpt": "1. The whole design, one example",
      "text": "The below brings up the possibility of \n`while a job is being completed...`\nfor transient things like the page hint",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-18T00:37:01.119Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "when the button is pressed",
      "offset": 1077,
      "edited": "2026-11-18T00:38:09.636Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-18T01:07:12.895Z",
          "html": "<p>Added as a during step:  what it sets lasts only while the call runs, and is put back when it ends, worked or failed.  Its words are round 2's Q18, <code>while completing a job</code> or yours, <code>while a job is being completed</code>.  It is in step 5 of the Server Actions plan.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-18T01:03:39.425Z"
      }
    },
